{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124157","id":4736429650,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGlAuUg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124157","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124157.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124157.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124157","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124157/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124157/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124157/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d48fb95d87cbefefe1070b5660ebf9c23a9234d2","number":124157,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GLES3: Allocate transform feedback output buffers as GL_DYNAMIC_COPY","user":{"login":"AbanoubNassem","id":13698722,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjk4NzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13698722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AbanoubNassem","html_url":"https://github.com/AbanoubNassem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AbanoubNassem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AbanoubNassem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AbanoubNassem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AbanoubNassem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AbanoubNassem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AbanoubNassem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AbanoubNassem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AbanoubNassem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AbanoubNassem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The GLES3 renderer skins (and blends) on the GPU with transform feedback into a per-instance vertex buffer, `MeshInstance::Surface::vertex_buffers[]`, that draws then read. The CPU never writes those buffers, but they were allocated `GL_DYNAMIC_DRAW` (the on-demand motion-vector buffer followed the source surface's `USE_DYNAMIC_UPDATE` flag). This PR allocates all three as `GL_DYNAMIC_COPY`, the hint the GL spec gives for \"modified repeatedly by GL, used as a source for GL drawing\".\n\n### Why it matters\n\nOn Windows, Compatibility runs through ANGLE's D3D11 backend on the GPUs Godot forces to ANGLE (and in every browser for the web export). ANGLE's D3D11 backend classifies `DYNAMIC_DRAW`/`STREAM_DRAW` as CPU-updated buffers (`BufferD3D::updateD3DBufferUsage`) and never binds such a buffer to the input assembler directly (`Buffer11::supportsDirectBinding()` is `usage == STATIC`). Every draw that reads a \"dynamic\" attribute re-streams it on the CPU (`VertexDataManager::storeDynamicAttribs` → `Buffer11::getData`), and because transform feedback marked the buffer written (`markTransformFeedbackUsage` → `invalidateStaticData`), `getData` first copies the GPU buffer back through a staging buffer with `Map(D3D11_MAP_READ)`. So every skinned body whose skeleton changed that frame costs a GPU readback and a CPU copy of its whole vertex buffer, per draw that reads it, and the buffer can never be promoted to static because the next frame's feedback pass writes it again.\n\nAll `*_COPY` and `*_READ` usages map to ANGLE's `STATIC` class, which binds the D3D11 buffer directly. The skinned layout (position `3 × float`, normal and tangent `2 × uint32` via `glVertexAttribIPointer`, 28-byte stride, 4-byte aligned offsets) needs no conversion, so `DirectStoragePossible` holds. Transform feedback already writes into ANGLE's `VERTEX_OR_TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK` D3D11 storage whatever the hint, so the draw now reads the same D3D11 buffer the feedback pass wrote.\n\n### Measurements (Godot 4.7.2 stable, Compatibility, Windows 11, GTX 780, i7-4770K, 1360×768)\n\nSame scene and camera, one hero plus 11 animated humanoid mobs and 3 NPCs (14 skinned bodies, 253 draws, 144k primitives), `RenderingServer.viewport_get_measured_render_time_cpu` per frame, each part measured by hiding it:\n\n| | native GL (`opengl3`) | ANGLE D3D11 (`opengl3_angle`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| whole frame render CPU | 1.63 ms | 9.9–10.2 ms |\n| the 11 mobs | ≈0.3 ms | 5.3–5.4 ms |\n| same 11 mobs, skeletons frozen (meshes still skinned and bound) | | ≈0 ms |\n| same 11 mobs drawn from their static mesh buffers (no skeleton) | | 0.1 ms |\n\nAbout 0.45 ms per re-skinned body per frame on that CPU, nothing for a skinned body whose bones did not change, so the cost is exactly the per-draw re-stream plus readback of the feedback-written buffer described above. Draw count, primitive count and GPU load did not move it.\n\n### Testing\n\nI have not yet benchmarked a build with this patch on D3D11; the numbers above are from the stock 4.7.2 template and isolate the mechanism (frozen skeleton = no feedback write = no cost). The patch builds and I will post a before/after from the same box once I have a Windows template with it. Native GL drivers only take the hint as advisory, so no change is expected there.\n\nHappy to split the motion-vector buffer change out if that line should keep following the surface's update flag.\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-04T18:00:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T10:57:20Z","closed_at":"2026-10-04T18:55:23Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d6f79f3eb805943fe0f647698fc2e2cd024661c1","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"AbanoubNas